 drinks outside the museum galleries.","short_summary":"Begin Saturday with a free public exhibition visit on campus.","evidence_claim":"The museum says it is always free and open to the public and lists Saturday hours of 10 a.m.–4 p.m., subject to holidays and university closures.","source_url":"https://mofa.fsu.edu/visitor-information/","source_title":"Visitor Information | FSU Museum of Fine Arts","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Saturday hours are listed as 10 a.m.–4 p.m.; check for holiday or university-closure changes. The museum is wheelchair accessible.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fsu-lakefront-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"FSU Lakefront Park & Retreat Center","title":"Take Saturday afternoon to Lake Bradford","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Outdoor recreation","notes":"Bring your FSUCard, swimwear and closed-toe shoes as needed; check weather and facility status before choosing a waterfront activity.","short_summary":"Shift from central campus to FSU’s lakefront recreation grounds.","evidence_claim":"FSU describes the Lakefront Park as a 73-acre Lake Bradford facility offering kayaking, paddleboarding, swimming, volleyball and disc golf; student kayak and paddleboard rentals are free.","source_url":"https://campusrec.fsu.edu/outdoors/lake/","source_title":"FSU Lakefront Park | FSU Campus Recreation","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-06-29","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The park is about four miles from main campus. Check current hours and weather status; alcohol is prohibited, and some activities have safety requirements.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fsu-garnet-gaming-lounge","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Garnet Gaming Lounge","title":"Return for consoles and tabletop games","subtitle":"Saturday evening · Askew Student Life Center","notes":"Stop inside the ASLC to compare available PC, console and tabletop options, then ask staff about access and current session procedures.","short_summary":"Choose a weather-proof social activity after the lakefront.","evidence_claim":"FSU identifies Garnet Gaming Lounge inside the Askew Student Life Center as a facility for PC, console and tabletop gaming.","source_url":"https://news.fsu.edu/news/students-campus-life/2025/09/19/fsus-garnet-gaming-lounge-to-host-grand-opening-celebration/","source_title":"FSU’s Garnet Gaming Lounge to host grand opening celebration","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-09-19","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located inside the Askew Student Life Center. Confirm current public hours, equipment availability and access rules before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fsu-strozier-library","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Robert Manning Strozier Library","title":"Scout a Sunday study base","subtitle":"Sunday midday · Academic reset","notes":"Walk the floors, identify a quiet zone and locate equipment or support services you may need once coursework starts in earnest.","short_summary":"Use a low-pressure visit to learn the main library before the week begins.","evidence_claim":"FSU says Strozier Library sits at the center of campus, has six floors, offers academic support, and provides computers, scanners, printers and equipment checkout.","source_url":"https://www.lib.fsu.edu/visit-and-study/strozier-library","source_title":"Robert Manning Strozier Library | University Libraries","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Bring an active FSUCard for turnstile entry and verify Sunday hours on the official library-hours page before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tallahassee-cascades-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Cascades Park","title":"Finish with a downtown park walk","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · Tallahassee orientation","notes":"Walk the park paths before sunset, note the historic survey marker, and use the outing to learn the route between campus and downtown.","short_summary":"Close the weekend by adding a civic landmark to your mental map.","evidence_claim":"The City of Tallahassee identifies Cascades Park at 1001 South Gadsden Street and states that park hours run from sunrise to sunset.","source_url":"https://www3.talgov.com/parks/parks-cascades-geninfo","source_title":"Cascades Park - General Information | City of Tallahassee","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Visit between sunrise and sunset. Follow posted park rules, keep out of waterways and check for event-related restrictions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
